Subject: [PATCH] dvbvideosink: NAL length prefixes become start codes also without a PTS

render() replaced the NAL length prefixes (stream-format avc, hvc1) with start codes only for the buffers with a valid
timestamp. GStreamer 1.28 h264parse gives avc to this sink for transport streams too; for interlaced H.264 coded as field
pairs, where the second field carries the PTS of the first one, the second field comes without PTS and was written with the
length prefixes: the decoder lost the second field of every reference picture (macro blocks on the whole picture).

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gstdvbvideosink.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gstdvbvideosink.c b/gstdvbvideosink.c
index 6df87e0..609528e 100644
--- a/gstdvbvideosink.c
+++ b/gstdvbvideosink.c
@@ -1057,13 +1057,20 @@ static GstFlowReturn gst_dvbvideosink_render(GstBaseSink *sink, GstBuffer *buffe
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (GST_BUFFER_PTS_IS_VALID(buffer) || (self->use_dts && GST_BUFFER_DTS_IS_VALID(buffer)))
+	gboolean has_timestamp = GST_BUFFER_PTS_IS_VALID(buffer) || (self->use_dts && GST_BUFFER_DTS_IS_VALID(buffer));
+	if (has_timestamp)
 	{
 		pes_header[7] = 0x80; /* pts */
 		pes_header[8] = 5; /* pts size */
 		pes_header_len += 5;
 		pes_set_pts(GST_BUFFER_PTS_IS_VALID(buffer) ? GST_BUFFER_PTS(buffer) : GST_BUFFER_DTS(buffer), pes_header);
+	}
 
+	/* NAL length prefixes (avc, hvc1) become start codes in every access unit, also in the ones without a timestamp: the
+	   second field of an interlaced picture can come with the PTS of the first field, and h264parse then pushes it without
+	   PTS. Written with the prefixes the decoder loses that field, so the reference pictures break (macro blocks). */
+	if (has_timestamp || ((self->codec_type == CT_H264 || self->codec_type == CT_H265) && self->h264_nal_len_size > 0))
+	{
 		if (self->codec_data)
 		{
 			if (self->must_send_header)
